# Sylva LMS UI Design Rule

Use this when building or restyling any page in `frontend/`.

## Visual foundation

- Page canvas uses `/body-bg.jpg` (light mode) via `--body-bg-image` in `main.css`. Do not leave large empty flat white regions.
- Dark mode: solid `--canvas`, no light background image.
- Content sits on translucent surfaces: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 94%, transparent)` + light `backdrop-filter`, border `var(--border)`, radius `12–14px`.
- Brand teal: `--brand` `#0f766e` (light) / `#44b5a8` (dark). Soft fill: `--brand-soft`.

## Typography

- Body: `IBM Plex Sans` via `--font-sans`. Display/titles: `IBM Plex Sans Condensed` via `--font-display`.
- Never fall back to Inter / Roboto / Arial / bare `system-ui` as primary.
- Base size ≥ 15px; body weight ≥ 500. Headings weight 700. Muted text uses `--text-muted` (readable, not washed out).
- Avoid ultra-thin weights and low-contrast gray-on-gray.

## Layout density

- Dashboards and admin lists should feel dense and professional: KPI strip + secondary pulse metrics + charts + side lists.
- One job per section; prefer CSS grid over card stacks.
- Panels: short title + one muted subtitle; charts/lists fill the panel.
- Keep first viewport purposeful (metrics + primary chart), not sparse hero marketing.

## Bilingual (vi / en)

- All user-facing strings go through `@nuxtjs/i18n` (`$t` / `t()`). Default locale: `vi`.
- Add keys to both `frontend/i18n/locales/vi.json` and `en.json` in the same PR/change.
- Menu labels use `admin.menu.*` keys from `admin-menu.ts` (`labelKey`), not hardcoded Vietnamese.
- Language switcher lives in admin topbar; locale persisted via cookie `sylva_locale`.

## Do / Don't

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD: token + i18n -->
<h2>{{ $t('admin.dashboard.trafficTitle') }}</h2>

<!-- ❌ BAD: system font + hardcoded copy -->
<h2 style="font-family: system-ui">Lưu lượng truy cập</h2>
```

- Do not invent a second color system or purple/indigo AI defaults.
- Do not place cards in heroes on public marketing pages; admin panels are OK as bordered surfaces.
